{"id":"n-20261015-eu8pe5","category":"finance","display_title":"US Inflation Rises to 3.7%","display_title_he":"האינפלציה בארצות הברית עולה ל-3.7 אחוזים","short_summary":"US inflation increased to 3.7% in September, creating political challenges for the Trump administration ahead of the midterm elections.","english_level":"C1","words":473,"reading_time":3,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Inflation_%281%29-_Economic_growth-es.png/960px-Inflation_%281%29-_Economic_growth-es.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"Jerine Victor · CC BY 4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Inflation_(1)-_Economic_growth-es.png"},"sources":[{"name":"The Guardian","domain":"theguardian.com","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/oct/14/inflation-numbers-september","title":"US inflation rose to 3.7% in September in blow to Republicans before midterms","published_at":"2026-10-14T14:29:42.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-14T14:29:42.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-15T06:01:52.776Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["The United States economy is facing renewed pressure as consumer prices accelerate just ahead of pivotal midterm elections. According to the Bureau of Labor Statistics, the annual inflation rate climbed to 3.7% in September, marking an increase from 3.4% in August and reaching its highest level since the spring. This final economic report delivers a significant political blow to the Trump administration, arriving amid widespread public dissatisfaction concerning the soaring cost of living.","Energy costs remain the primary driver behind the surge in consumer prices, largely influenced by the ongoing US-Israel war with Iran. Government data reveals that gasoline prices have jumped 34% compared to the previous year, accounting for over half of overall price increases, while fuel oil, essential for residential heating, surged by 74%, posing a worrying sign for households heading into the winter. Furthermore, air travel expenses experienced a 22.4% increase. Research from Brown University indicates that these elevated energy expenses have cost American consumers a total of $133 billion, averaging more than $1,020 per household. Diesel, which powers domestic supply chains, also reached a record high last month, and average gas prices remain over a dollar per gallon higher than last year according to AAA.","Public frustration is increasingly directed toward lawmakers and the White House, with Republicans entering the elections facing the highest rate of inflation since the spring, excluding the pandemic, since 1990. A recent survey conducted by Reuters/Ipsos demonstrates that 78% of Americans attribute the high inflation rates, which continue to outpace personal earnings, to current government policies. Even among registered Republicans who support Donald Trump, 57% expressed blame toward the administration.","In response to these economic pressures, President Trump has defended his administration's record while pointing outward for external causes. During a political rally in Wasilla, Alaska, he maintained that his support for families has been substantial and argued that political opponents repeatedly weaponize the issue of affordability. Additionally, he suggested on social media that foreign actors, including Yemen's Houthi group acting at the behest of Iran, deliberately targeted Saudi Arabia in a deliberate effort to drive up oil prices prior to the American elections in a way that is not nice. Meanwhile, the White House did not immediately respond to a request for comment on the latest report.","Economic analysts note that persistent inflation and soaring energy expenses continue to deplete household budgets, making the economy a top issue for voters. The Federal Reserve previously raised interest rates in an effort to cool elevated prices, pushing the 30-year mortgage rate up to 7.40%. Financial experts, such as Richard Carter from Quilter Cheviot, observe that despite various measures from the administration, such as permitting Russian diesel back into the market in a desperate bid to get inflation under control and provide an environment for rate cuts, global market pressures stemming from the Middle East conflict continue to exert a powerful grip on the domestic economy."],"facts":[{"fact":"US inflation rose to an annual rate of 3.7% in September, up from 3.4% in August, according to the Bureau of Labor Statistics.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Gasoline prices increased by 34% from last year, while fuel oil rose by 74% and air travel by 22.4%.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Energy price increases are largely driven by the US-Israel war with Iran.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Brown University data shows higher energy prices have cost American households over $1,020 on average.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"A Reuters/Ipsos survey indicates 78% of Americans blame the Trump administration's policies for inflation outpacing earnings.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"United States","lemma":"United States","pos":"PROPN","he":"ארצות הברית","name":"location"},{"text":"economy","lemma":"economy","pos":"NOUN","he":"כַּלְכָּלָה","name":null},{"text":"facing","lemma":"face","pos":"VERB","he":"מִתְאוֹדֵד עִם","name":null},{"text":"renewed","lemma":"renewed","pos":"ADJ","he":"מְחֻדָּשׁ","name":null},{"text":"pressure","lemma":"pressure","pos":"NOUN","he":"לַחַץ","name":null},{"text":"consumer prices","lemma":"consumer price","pos":"NOUN","he":"מְחִירֵי צְרִיכָה","name":null},{"text":"accelerate","lemma":"accelerate","pos":"VERB","he":"לְהָאץ","name":null},{"text":"ahead","lemma":"ahead","pos":"ADV","he":"לִקְרַאת","name":null},{"text":"pivotal","lemma":"pivotal","pos":"ADJ","he":"קְרִיטִי / מַכְרִיעַ","name":null},{"text":"midterm elections","lemma":"midterm election","pos":"NOUN","he":"בְּחִירוֹת אֶמְצַע כְּהֻנָּה","name